b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 648.5 Td (Q.5 \(a\) State the Four Necessary Conditions for Deadlock. Explain Banker's Algorithm ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 635.0 Td (    with a safety check example. [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 621.5 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 608.0 Td (Four Necessary Conditions \(Coffman Conditions\):) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 594.5 Td (1. Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource must be held in a non-shareable mode.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 581.0 Td (2. Hold and Wait: A process holds at least one resource and waits for additional reso) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 567.5 Td (    urces held by others.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 554.0 Td (3. No Preemption: Resources cannot be forcibly confiscated from a process; only relea) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 540.5 Td (    sed voluntarily.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 527.0 Td (4. Circular Wait: A closed chain of processes P0, P1, ..., Pn exists such that P0 wai) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 513.5 Td (    ts for P1, and Pn waits for P0.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 500.0 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 486.5 Td (Banker's Algorithm:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 473.0 Td (Given 3 resource types: A\(10\), B\(5\), C\(7\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 459.5 Td (Available Vector: Available = Total - sum\(Allocation\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 446.0 Td (Need Matrix = Max - Allocation.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 432.5 Td (A process Pi can be executed if Need_i <= Available. Once executed, Available = Avail) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 419.0 Td (    able + Allocation_i.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 405.5 Td (If all processes complete, the system is in a SAFE STATE.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 392.0 Td () Tj
